	{"@id":"gpc:30006706","type":"gpc:AttributeValue","label_en":"EWES MILK"},
	{"@id":"gpc:30015580","type":"gpc:AttributeValue","label_en":"COOKING POTS AND PANS","comment_en":"This term is used to describe products that manufacture has specifically designed for cooking pots and pans."},
	{"@id":"gpc:30016118","type":"gpc:AttributeValue","label_en":"MORTEAU","comment_en":"Morteau Sausage, also known as the Belle de Morteau, is a pork sausage traditional smoked pork sausage from the Morteau region of France (Haut-Doubs). It is a very strongly flavoured and very dense uncooked sausage. This sausage is smoked for at least 48 hours using sawdust made from conifer and juniper plants. It is not cooked, however, as the combustion is accompanied by a strong current of air. It is usually identifiable by the wooden peg/plug which is closing one of its end and sometimes with an escutcheon with the name of the manufacturer."},
	{"@id":"gpc:30016448","type":"gpc:AttributeValue","label_en":"FRANCE - BURGUNDY - BIENVENUES-BATARD-MONTRACHET"},
	{"@id":"gpc:30018502","type":"gpc:AttributeValue","label_en":"GERMANY - W&#220;RTTEMBERG"},
